WEBVTT

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:09.800
People at the CIA are there for 25, 30, 35 years.

00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:11.000
They're unelected.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:13.700
There's no accountability to pretty much anyone.

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:16.700
And they know that they can outweigh presidents.

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:18.700
If there's a president that they don't like,

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:21.200
like Donald Trump, they don't have to do what he says.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:24.700
They just slow-roll whatever orders come from the White House

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:30.150
and end up at Langley.

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:33.650
If there's one lesson that I learned at the CIA,

00:00:33.650 --> 00:00:36.950
it's that the CIA will push the envelope

00:00:36.950 --> 00:00:41.250
all the way into illegality unless somebody pushes back.

00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:51.380
I have said is that this campaign

00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:55.280
is not just about electing a president.

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:59.680
It is about making a political revolution.

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:04.410
And tea.

00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:08.410
Taking money from our children

00:01:08.410 --> 00:01:11.210
and borrowing from China.

00:01:11.210 --> 00:01:14.760
People are dying.

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:16.460
Is the program so critical

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:18.460
it's worth borrowing money from China to pay for it?

00:01:18.460 --> 00:01:19.960
And if not, I'll get rid of it.

00:01:19.960 --> 00:01:28.730
Stop lying and the truth!

00:01:28.730 --> 00:01:38.540
Avoid the apocalypse altogether.

00:01:38.540 --> 00:01:40.840
Here's another episode of Macro and Cheese

00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:43.040
with your host, Steve Grumbine.

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:43.640
All right.

00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:47.940
Yes, this is Steve Grumbine with Macro and Cheese this week.

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:50.840
I have another whistleblower.

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:53.540
I've got a guy who has been on the inside

00:01:53.540 --> 00:01:56.240
seen what the belly of the beast looks like,

00:01:56.240 --> 00:02:00.340
came outside and has not been able to stop talking about it since.

00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:02.640
I'm speaking about John Kiriakou,

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:04.740
who is a former CIA officer,

00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:08.640
former senior investigator for the Senate Farm Relations Committee

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:13.140
and former counterterrorism consultant for ABC News.

00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:17.440
He was responsible for the capture in Pakistan in 2002

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:19.940
of Abu Zabudai,

00:02:19.940 --> 00:02:23.840
believed to be the third ranking official in Al Qaeda.

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:28.840
In 2007, Kiriakou blew the whistle on the CIA's torture program,

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:31.140
saying the CIA tortured prisoners

00:02:31.140 --> 00:02:34.640
that torture was official U.S. government policy

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:40.540
and that the policy had been approved by then-President George W. Bush.

00:02:40.540 --> 00:02:43.140
He became the sixth whistleblower indicted

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:47.040
by the Obama administration under the Espionage Act,

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:49.840
a law designed to punish spies.

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:54.340
He served 23 months in prison as a result of the revelation.

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:57.440
Kiriakou won the Joseph A. Callaway Award

00:02:57.440 --> 00:03:00.040
for Civic Courage in 2012,

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:05.140
Penn Center USA's prestigious First Amendment Award in 2015,

00:03:05.140 --> 00:03:09.240
the first blueprint for free speech international whistleblowing prize

00:03:09.240 --> 00:03:13.640
for bravery and integrity in the public interest in 2016,

00:03:13.640 --> 00:03:17.940
and the Sam Adams Award for integrity and intelligence,

00:03:17.940 --> 00:03:20.540
also in 2016.

00:03:20.540 --> 00:03:23.340
Kiriakou is the author of The Reluctant Spy,

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:26.440
My Secret Life in the CIA's War on Terror,

00:03:26.440 --> 00:03:29.440
doing time like a spy,

00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:33.440
how the CIA taught me to survive and thrive in prison,

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:37.840
and the convenient terrorist and Abu Zabadi

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:41.440
and the weird wonderland of America's secret wars.

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:45.140
And without further ado, let me bring on my guest, John.

00:03:45.140 --> 00:03:46.840
Welcome to the show, sir.

00:03:46.840 --> 00:03:47.640
Thank you, Steve.

00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:48.940
Good to be with you.

