was a senator who had kind of left you high and dry

00:05:33.540 --> 00:05:36.540
during your time when you had come out and been brave

00:05:36.540 --> 00:05:38.340
and he ignored you.

00:05:38.340 --> 00:05:40.540
And when you confronted him with it,

00:05:40.540 --> 00:05:43.540
his concern was that he was going to lose his clearance

00:05:43.540 --> 00:05:45.740
that the CIA had eyes on him

00:05:45.740 --> 00:05:48.580
and that terror that he felt,

00:05:48.580 --> 00:05:51.880
the way I understand it based on some of your work,

00:05:51.880 --> 00:05:54.780
seems like that's not a isolated incident.

00:05:54.780 --> 00:05:58.280
That seems to be like an unelected body

00:05:58.280 --> 00:06:01.780
is hovering over our elected representatives.

00:06:01.780 --> 00:06:04.980
And so beyond the idea of democracy failing us,

00:06:04.980 --> 00:06:08.680
there's a deep state that control the levers of power

00:06:08.680 --> 00:06:12.480
that go beyond the theater that is politics.

00:06:12.480 --> 00:06:14.980
So often, Steve, people believe

00:06:14.980 --> 00:06:16.980
that this is a right-wing trope

00:06:16.980 --> 00:06:18.180
and it's not.

00:06:18.180 --> 00:06:22.980
It's a fact of everyday life here in the United States.

00:06:22.980 --> 00:06:26.780
The week that Donald Trump became president

