let's say they just move slowly,

00:07:55.680 --> 00:07:58.580
knowing that in four years he's going to be gone

00:07:58.580 --> 00:08:01.780
or worst case scenario, eight years he's going to be gone.

00:08:01.780 --> 00:08:03.980
Now, one of the other things that the CIA does

00:08:03.980 --> 00:08:05.980
and they're very, very good at this

00:08:05.980 --> 00:08:10.280
is recruiting in air quotes, recruiting new presidents.

00:08:10.280 --> 00:08:14.980
The CIA especially loves it when a president is elected

00:08:14.980 --> 00:08:18.880
who has little or no intelligence experience.

00:08:18.880 --> 00:08:23.180
Because what happens is literally the day after the election,

00:08:23.180 --> 00:08:26.980
the PDB staff, the president's daily brief staff begins

00:08:26.980 --> 00:08:30.780
to brief the new president-elect

00:08:30.780 --> 00:08:33.780
with the same briefing that the president himself gets.

00:08:33.780 --> 00:08:36.080
Now, when I was there, there were only 11 people

00:08:36.080 --> 00:08:39.180
who were entitled to a daily PDB briefing.

00:08:39.180 --> 00:08:40.980
So it's the president, the vice president,

00:08:40.980 --> 00:08:43.580
the secretaries of state and defense,

00:08:43.580 --> 00:08:45.580
the National Security Advisor,

00:08:45.580 --> 00:08:48.680
a handful of people in the National Security Council

00:08:48.680 --> 00:08:50.680
and that's pretty much it.

00:08:50.680 --> 00:08:55.580
So when you've got a brand new young, inexperienced president,

00:08:55.580 --> 00:08:58.080
you go to him the day after the election

00:08:58.080 --> 00:09:00.380
or her, whatever the case happens to be

